# What is committed here is LF. `core.autocrlf` is true on the dev box and does
# NOT normalise these repos on the way in, so state it rather than trusting the
# heuristic: a pure-CRLF source file has been measured staging as a
# 236-insertion whole-file rewrite over a five-line change, which buries the
# real edit. See the root CLAUDE.md, "Write LF into the magmacrunch repos".
#
# Deliberately NO blanket `eol=lf`. `apps/magmacrunch` and `apps/media-player`
# both argue against pinning checkout, on the grounds that what is committed is
# LF whatever a clone does on disk, and this follows them. `text=auto` is the
# half that matters.
#
# Later rules win, so the general case is first and the exceptions follow.
* text=auto

# These break outright rather than merely looking untidy: a trailing CR on a
# shebang gives "bad interpreter", and a workflow's `run:` block is handed to a
# Linux shell verbatim. Pinned even where the repo has none yet, because the
# first one added should not have to remember this file exists.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
